WEBVTT

00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:08.209
[dragon roars in distance]

00:00:08.384 --> 00:00:10.908
Come on.
Give me something to shoot at.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:14.041
- Give me something
to shoot at.
- [dragon roars]

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:19.743
[dragon approaching]

00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:25.270
[dragon divebombing]

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:28.404
- [weapon fires]
- Aah!

00:00:30.231 --> 00:00:32.756
[dragon roars]

00:00:34.235 --> 00:00:36.934
I hit it. Yes, I hit it!

00:00:37.108 --> 00:00:39.197
- Did anybody see that?
- [growls]

00:00:40.328 --> 00:00:41.721
Except for you.

00:00:43.897 --> 00:00:46.683
[Hiccup screaming]

00:00:46.857 --> 00:00:50.121
- [sighs] Do not
let them escape!
- [man] Right!

00:00:50.295 --> 00:00:52.297
- [dragon growling]
- [screams]

00:00:53.603 --> 00:00:55.822
[panting]

00:00:55.996 --> 00:00:57.389
[dragon growls]

00:01:03.961 --> 00:01:05.353
[roars]

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.835
[burps]

00:01:09.009 --> 00:01:10.054
You're all out.

00:01:10.228 --> 00:01:11.751
[grunting]

00:01:16.669 --> 00:01:19.237
[Hiccup] Oh, and there's
one more thing
you need to know.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.285
[screams]

00:01:26.636 --> 00:01:29.203
- [woman yells]
- [metal torch clanging]

00:01:29.377 --> 00:01:31.771
- [glass breaks]
- Sorry, Dad.

00:01:31.945 --> 00:01:34.470
- [screaming]
- [sheep braying]

00:01:37.995 --> 00:01:40.040
[dragons growling]

00:01:41.346 --> 00:01:43.522
OK, but I hit
a Night Fury. Aah!

00:01:43.696 --> 00:01:45.829
It's not like
the last few times, Dad!

00:01:46.003 --> 00:01:47.526
I really, actually hit it!

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.355
You guys were busy.
I had a very clear shot.

00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:53.880
It went down off Raven Point.
Let's get a search party...

00:01:54.054 --> 00:01:57.797
Stop! Just stop.

00:01:57.971 --> 00:02:00.757
Every time you step outside,
disaster follows.

00:02:00.931 --> 00:02:03.150
Can you not see that
I have bigger problems?

00:02:03.324 --> 00:02:06.414
Winter is almost here
and I have an entire
village to feed!

00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:11.855
Between you and me,
the village could do with
a little less feeding.

00:02:12.029 --> 00:02:13.944
This isn't a joke,
Hiccup!

00:02:14.118 --> 00:02:17.425
[groans] Why can't you
follow the simplest orders?

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.169
I can't stop myself.
I see a dragon and I have
to just kill it.

00:02:22.343 --> 00:02:24.171
It's who I am, Dad.

00:02:24.345 --> 00:02:26.957
Oh, you're many things,
Hiccup.

00:02:27.131 --> 00:02:29.829
But a dragon killer
is not one of them.

00:02:30.003 --> 00:02:31.004
Get back to the house.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:33.050
Make sure he gets there.

00:02:34.225 --> 00:02:36.488
I have his mess
to clean up.

00:02:36.662 --> 00:02:39.012
- [girl laughing]
- Quite the performance.

00:02:39.186 --> 00:02:41.058
I've never seen anyone
mess up that badly.
That helped.

00:02:41.232 --> 00:02:43.451
Thank you, thank you.
I was trying.

00:02:44.365 --> 00:02:46.106
Ow! [grunts]

00:02:48.413 --> 00:02:50.371
- I really did hit one.
- [Gobber] Sure, Hiccup.

00:02:50.546 --> 00:02:52.504
- He never listens.
- It runs in the family.

00:02:52.678 --> 00:02:55.507
When he does, it's with
this disappointed scowl,

00:02:55.681 --> 00:02:57.901
like someone skimped
on meat in his sandwich.

00:02:58.075 --> 00:02:59.555
[mimics Stoick]
"Excuse me, barmaid.

00:02:59.729 --> 00:03:02.427
I'm afraid you brought me
the wrong offspring.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.082
I ordered an extra-large boy
with beefy arms,

00:03:05.256 --> 00:03:07.301
extra guts and glory
on the side.

00:03:07.475 --> 00:03:10.087
This here, this is
a talking fishbone."

00:03:10.261 --> 00:03:12.350
You're thinking
about this wrong.

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:14.395
It's not so much
what you look like,

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.528
it's what's inside
that he can't stand.

00:03:18.095 --> 00:03:20.227
Thank you
for summing that up.

00:03:20.401 --> 00:03:23.883
Look, the point is,
stop trying so hard to be
something you're not.

00:03:24.057 --> 00:03:25.537
I just want to be
one of you guys.

00:03:26.712 --> 00:03:28.540
- [door closes]
- [sighs]

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.464
[Stoick] Either we finish them
or they'll finish us!

00:03:39.638 --> 00:03:42.119
It's the only way
we'll be rid of them.

00:03:42.293 --> 00:03:44.338
If we find the nest
and destroy it,

00:03:44.512 --> 00:03:47.472
the dragons will leave.
They'll find another home!

00:03:47.646 --> 00:03:50.127
One more search
before the ice sets in.

00:03:50.301 --> 00:03:52.433
Those ships
never come back.

00:03:52.608 --> 00:03:57.090
We're Vikings. It's
an occupational hazard.
Now who's with me?!

00:03:57.264 --> 00:03:59.005
[man] Count me out.

00:03:59.179 --> 00:04:00.703
- Today's no good for me.
- I have to do my axe returns.

00:04:00.877 --> 00:04:03.662
All right. Those who stay
will look after Hiccup.

00:04:03.836 --> 00:04:05.185
- [woman] To the ships!
- [man] I'm with you!

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:06.491
Aye.
That's more like it.

00:04:08.101 --> 00:04:10.321
Right.
I'll pack my undies.

00:04:10.495 --> 00:04:13.280
No, I need you to stay
and train some new recruits.

00:04:13.454 --> 00:04:17.676
Perfect. And, while I'm busy,
Hiccup can cover the stall.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.332
Molten steel,
razor-sharp blades,
lots of time to himself.

00:04:21.506 --> 00:04:23.595
What could possibly
go wrong?

00:04:23.769 --> 00:04:25.858
[groans] What am I going
to do with him, Gobber?

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.207
Put him in training.

00:04:27.381 --> 00:04:29.514
- No, I'm serious.
- So am I.

00:04:29.688 --> 00:04:32.473
He'd be killed
before the first dragon
is out of its cage.

00:04:32.648 --> 00:04:34.214
- You don't know that.
- I do, actually.

00:04:34.388 --> 00:04:35.607
- No, you don't.
- No, I do.

00:04:35.781 --> 00:04:37.348
No, you don't.

00:04:37.522 --> 00:04:39.219
Listen,
you know what he's like.

00:04:39.393 --> 00:04:43.310
From the time he could crawl,
he's been... different.

00:04:43.484 --> 00:04:45.008
[sighs] He doesn't listen.

00:04:45.182 --> 00:04:48.228
He has the attention
span of a sparrow.

00:04:48.402 --> 00:04:51.536
I take him fishing and
he goes hunting for trolls!

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.539
Trolls exist.
They steal your socks.

00:04:54.713 --> 00:04:57.498
But only the left ones.
What's with that?

00:04:57.673 --> 00:04:59.065
- When I was a boy...
- Here we go.

00:04:59.239 --> 00:05:00.545
...my father told me

00:05:00.719 --> 00:05:02.329
to bang my head against
a rock and I did it.

00:05:02.503 --> 00:05:04.941
I thought it was crazy,
but I didn't question him.

00:05:05.115 --> 00:05:07.160
- And you know what happened?
- You got a headache.

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.728
That rock split in two.

00:05:09.902 --> 00:05:12.688
It taught me what
a Viking could do, Gobber.

00:05:12.862 --> 00:05:16.692
He could crush mountains,
level forests, tame seas!

00:05:18.171 --> 00:05:20.217
Even as a boy,
I knew what I was,

00:05:20.391 --> 00:05:21.697
what I had to become.

00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:24.482
Hiccup is not that boy.

00:05:24.656 --> 00:05:27.180
You can't stop him,
Stoick.

00:05:27.354 --> 00:05:30.009
You can only prepare him.

00:05:30.183 --> 00:05:34.274
I know it seems hopeless,
but you won't always be
around to protect him.

00:05:34.448 --> 00:05:37.669
He's going to get
out there again.
He's probably out there now.

00:05:40.237 --> 00:05:42.152
[birds singing in distance]

00:05:47.244 --> 00:05:48.506
[deep breath]

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.160
[exhales]

00:05:55.469 --> 00:05:58.646
[sighs]
Oh, the gods hate me.

00:05:58.821 --> 00:06:01.301
Some people lose their knife
or their mug. Not me.

00:06:01.475 --> 00:06:04.435
I manage to lose
an entire dragon.

00:06:05.566 --> 00:06:07.046
Ow!

00:06:11.181 --> 00:06:13.444
[bird calling, faint]

